window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-e75eca413fc42dd3"]={"key":"ny_b1-e75eca413fc42dd3","group":"ny_b1","uid":"e75eca413fc42dd3","rank":30,"title":"elmsworth hosted erp negotiation position","occupation":"computer_information_systems_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Aleksy Calderon, the information systems manager at Elmsworth Solutions responsible for the weighbridge and grain-trading platform used by Ravensmoor Agricultural. The ERP vendor will retire its on-premises edition in eleven months and has quoted a hosted migration at 2.3 times current annual maintenance. Your renegotiation call is on 22 September, with Ravensmoor finance director Sasha Rasmussen attending alongside vendor commercial and technical staff. Your first draft came back from Pascal Duarte because it described the migration but did not give you a position you could actually hold on the call, and it blurred which commitments belong to technology, finance and legal. Since then, the vendor has said a phased go-live is possible but that data extraction at exit would be separately charged. Elmsworth policy requires Ravensmoor's operational data to remain practically exportable in a documented, usable format and does not permit uncapped recurring commitments. Sasha has authorised three-year subscription charges, excluding one-time migration services, up to an average of 1.75 times current annual maintenance; do not invent the underlying spend or unsupported vendor figures, and express financial positions as multiples or clearly labelled assumptions. Prepare a revised negotiation position that gives one opening ask, an ordered concession sequence, a clear walk-away response and exactly one term that never moves. Project the commercial effect under the assumptions you choose so Sasha can understand the tradeoffs. The platform supports sites in England and the Republic of Ireland, while the hosting proposal does not yet identify all processing locations or include final data-protection terms. Mark where finance or legal validation is required rather than deciding those functions' issues yourself. Sasha is not a cloud or privacy specialist, but the vendor participants are, so keep the language accessible without turning the memo into an ERP, hosting or GDPR tutorial. Produce no more than five slides, with no appendix, and write the finished presentation to the top level of your working directory using exactly the filename `negotiation_position.pptx`.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `negotiation_position.pptx` — A concise, non-specialist negotiation position memorandum presented as slides for the 22 September hosted-ERP renegotiation call. (Maximum five slides with no appendix. It must state one opening ask, an ordered concession sequence, a walk-away response, exactly one non-negotiable term, scenario-based commercial implications, and appropriate finance and legal boundaries.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/negotiation_position.pptx","bytes":40643,"extension":".pptx","url":"assets/affc041a144441fcb12248533c91ff806828c6f266eae143fd3c33273e67ce4c.pptx","sha256":"affc041a144441fcb12248533c91ff806828c6f266eae143fd3c33273e67ce4c","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"=== 幻灯片 1 ===\nDECISION MEMO  /  22 SEPTEMBER\nHold a bounded position\nfor Ravensmoor's hosted ERP move\nAleksy Calderon  |  Information Systems Manager  |  Elmsworth Solutions\nSITUATION\nVendor retires the on-premises edition in 11 months and has quoted hosted migration at 2.3× current annual maintenance.\nKNOWN FACTS\n•  Sites in England + Republic of Ireland\n•  Phased go-live is possible\n•  Exit extraction is separately charged today\nAUTHORITY\nThree-year average subscription ≤ 1.75×M.\nOne-time migration services sit outside that ceiling and need separate control.\nCALL OUTCOME\nOpen once, trade in order, and do not accept a commitment outside Aleksy's envelope.\nM = current annual maintenance (normalized unit; no underlying spend assumed).\nElmsworth Solutions  |  Internal call brief\n01 / 05\n\n=== 幻灯片 2 ===\n01  /  OPENING POSITION\nOne package to put first\nA credible anchor below Sasha's ceiling, with terms that control delivery and exit.\nOPENING ASK\n1.30× M\nthree-year average\nIllustrative path: 1.25× / 1.30× / 1.35× M\nPut this package first. It leaves room to move while staying below the authorised 1.75× average.\nPOSITION, not a vendor commitment\nTHE PACKAGE\nPrice  \nThree-year subscription path above; no uncapped renewal escalator. Proposed cap: 3% annually.\nTransition  \nPhased go-live plan, named vendor transition lead, and milestone acceptance.\nServices  \nMigration services priced once, itemised and agreed separately from recurring subscription.\nContinuity  \nService levels with meaningful credits; hosting locations and final data-protection terms supplied for review.\nNever trade away the protected exit term on slide 5.\nElmsworth Solutions  |  Internal call brief\n02 / 05\n\n=== 幻灯片 3 ===\n02  /  LIVE-CALL LADDER\nTrade only in this order\nEvery Elmsworth move buys a specific vendor return. Exit-related flexibility starts only after two vendor concessions.\n1\nReference call\nELMSWORTH GIVES\nBounded customer reference: one call, pre-approved message, no logo use.\nVENDOR MUST GIVE\nVendor lowers average to 1.25×M and caps annual uplift at 2.5%.\n2\nPhased go-live\nELMSWORTH GIVES\nAccept a phased schedule if operational cutover criteria are written.\nVENDOR MUST GIVE\nVendor fixes migration scope/price, names a lead and adds milestone acceptance.\n3\nExit rehearsal\nELMSWORTH GIVES\nAfter rungs 1–2 only: allow a quarterly export rehearsal and data-mapping workshop.\nVENDOR MUST GIVE\nVendor funds the rehearsal, provides 90-day exit assistance and documents processing locations.\n4\nCase study\nELMSWORTH GIVES\nOnly if still needed: a controlled, anonymised case study after go-live.\nVENDOR MUST GIVE\nVendor moves to ≤1.55×M average, keeps the finite 3% cap and adds service credits.\nStop the ladder if the return is not written into the order form, schedule or contract change.\nElmsworth Solutions  |  Internal call brief\n03 / 05\n\n=== 幻灯片 4 ===\n03  /  NORMALIZED COMMERCIAL EFFECT\nThree-year view using M\nSame baseline and period make the trade-off visible to Finance; migration services are shown separately.\nIllustrative subscription-only scenarios  |  M = current annual maintenance\nSCENARIO\nYEAR 1 → YEAR 3\n3-YEAR TOTAL\nAVERAGE / YEAR\nVendor quote (known)\n2.30 → 2.30 → 2.30×M\n6.90×M\n2.30×M\nProposed opening (position)\n1.25 → 1.30 → 1.35×M\n3.90×M\n1.30×M\nINDICATIVE DIFFERENCE\n3.00×M less over three years  |  43.5% below quote\nASSUMPTIONS TO TEST\nQuote shown at 0% escalation because none was supplied. Opening path uses 3% cap as a proposed term. One-time migration services excluded from both totals and need a separate fixed quote.\nThe 11-month deadline gives the vendor leverage; conditional commitment, scope gates and written acceptance preserve ours.\nElmsworth Solutions  |  Internal call brief\n04 / 05\n\n=== 幻灯片 5 ===\n04  /  BOUNDARIES AND CLOSE\nOne term never moves; everything else needs an owner\nUse this wording to stop accidental acceptance and keep Finance and Legal in their lanes.\nNON-NEGOTIABLE\nAt exit, Ravensmoor operational data must be practically exportable in a documented, usable format with no separate extraction fee.\nCALL CONTROL\nIf that term is refused, say: “We cannot accept this hosted renewal. I will pause today and request a written counterproposal; no commitment is authorised.”\nFINANCE  /  SASHA\nAleksy may trade within the 1.75×M three-year average envelope. Sasha must approve any over-ceiling exposure before signature. Finance validates the separate migration-services quote.\nLEGAL VALIDATION\nEngland: UK GDPR + Data Protection Act 2018. Republic of Ireland: EU GDPR + Irish supervisory context. Processing locations, transfer arrangements and final DPA terms are unresolved; Legal reviews before acceptance.\nDO NOT CONFUSE LOCATION WITH LAWFUL TRANSFER\nResidency alone does not settle international access. Privacy paperwork complements, but does not replace, contractual exit, continuity and migration-assistance terms.\nMandate: open at 1.30×M average, trade only in order, and stop if fee-free usable export is absent.\nElmsworth Solutions  |  Internal call brief\n05 / 05","truncated":false,"note":"PPTX 共5页的文字提取；不还原位置、动画和版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required PowerPoint file exists at the submitted top level, opens successfully and is a valid presentation rather than a renamed or corrupt file.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"The submitted file and its internal Office document structure.","grader_hint":"Open `negotiation_position.pptx` and verify that the package is structurally valid and its slides can be read."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation contains no more than five slides and does not add an appendix.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Slide count, slide titles and any appendix labeling.","grader_hint":"Count all slides, including hidden slides, and confirm that none is presented as an appendix."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered slides are legible at normal presentation scale, with no clipped, overlapping or materially off-canvas content.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered slide images or PDF output.","grader_hint":"Render every slide and inspect for clipping, overlaps, unreadably small text and content extending beyond slide boundaries."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation is understandable to Sasha Rasmussen without assuming cloud-contracting, ERP-migration or privacy-law expertise.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Language, definitions, visual hierarchy and treatment of specialist terms throughout the deck.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a finance director outside IT could understand the position, tradeoffs and call boundaries without asking for specialist interpretation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation identifies the 22 September renegotiation, Elmsworth Solutions, Ravensmoor Agricultural and the hosted-ERP decision context.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening context or title material.","grader_hint":"Look for the date, both organisations and an unambiguous description of the negotiation being prepared for."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The commercial context correctly links the vendor's 2.3-times-maintenance quote to the on-premises edition ending support in eleven months.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Situation summary and any commercial baseline shown.","grader_hint":"Confirm that both supplied facts are present and related correctly; the deck must not reverse the timing or present 2.3x as an agreed price."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation states the authorised ceiling as a three-year average subscription charge no greater than 1.75 times current annual maintenance and keeps one-time migration services outside that ceiling.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority, guardrail or financial-position content.","grader_hint":"Verify the period, 1.75x multiple and exclusion of one-time migration services. Do not accept a generic budget reference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Known facts, proposed negotiation positions and projection assumptions are distinguishable from one another.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labels, wording, footnotes and scenario presentation.","grader_hint":"Check that the vendor quote and timing are treated as known facts, while target terms and forecast assumptions are not presented as existing vendor commitments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck presents exactly one clearly identifiable opening commercial ask rather than several competing opening positions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening-position wording and any summary or call script.","grader_hint":"A package may contain several linked terms, but there must be one coherent package to put first to the vendor, not alternative openings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The opening ask is numerically anchored below the authorised ceiling, leaves bargaining room and is framed as a credible package rather than an unsupported demand.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening price multiple, term package and supporting rationale.","grader_hint":"Assess whether the opening target is below 1.75x, commercially intelligible and capable of being defended using the migration situation without fabricated market evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The opening package addresses the material dimensions of hosted migration rather than reducing the negotiation to headline subscription price alone.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Terms included in the opening package.","grader_hint":"Look for a compact treatment of recurring price, escalation, implementation or transition, service commitments and exit/data access. Equivalent commercially material terms are acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Exactly one term is expressly designated as non-negotiable, immovable or a walk-away condition.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Guardrail wording, call script and summary conclusion.","grader_hint":"Count only terms explicitly elevated to the never-move status. Other boundaries may be stated, but the deck must not label multiple terms as co-equal non-negotiables."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The chosen non-negotiable protects practical export of Ravensmoor operational data at exit in a documented, usable format without a separate extraction fee.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Non-negotiable language and supporting rationale.","grader_hint":"Full credit requires all three elements: practical export, a documented usable format and no separate extraction charge. Mere ownership language or a promise to discuss exit later is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The position rejects an uncapped renewal escalator and substitutes a bounded mechanism, such as a fixed cap or a capped objective index.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Renewal or price-adjustment term in the opening position and guardrails.","grader_hint":"Confirm that recurring increases cannot become unlimited. If an index is used, it must have an explicit cap or equivalent finite boundary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Concessions are shown in an explicit order that Aleksy can follow live rather than as an unordered menu.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Numbered sequence, ladder or equivalent progression.","grader_hint":"The deck must make the next permitted move clear at each stage. A list of possible trades without order does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Reference-call or customer-advocacy rights are treated as a relatively low-cost Elmsworth concession and exchanged for a meaningful vendor improvement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"A concession rung involving reference participation or an equivalent bounded advocacy commitment.","grader_hint":"Look for reasonable controls on the commitment and a specific vendor return, such as price, escalation, service or implementation improvement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Phased go-live flexibility is used as a priced negotiating variable rather than accepted for free or mistaken for an unconditional vendor concession.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Treatment of migration phasing in the concession sequence.","grader_hint":"The deck should state what Elmsworth can flex and what it receives in exchange, while preserving operationally necessary safeguards."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each offered concession is conditional on an identified reciprocal vendor concession of credible value.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The give/get relationship at every rung of the concession sequence.","grader_hint":"Walk the sequence line by line. Full credit requires a clear vendor return for every Elmsworth move, not merely an overall aspiration at the end."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No negotiable exit-related value is offered until the vendor has made at least two distinct concessions, while the core fee-free usable-export term remains protected throughout.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Order and content of the concession ladder.","grader_hint":"Identify the first exit-related Elmsworth movement and count prior vendor concessions. There must be at least two, and no rung may surrender the core non-negotiable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The walk-away response is operationally usable: it tells Aleksy what not to authorise on the call and what controlled response to give if the vendor will not meet the boundary.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Walk-away language or live-call script.","grader_hint":"Accept a pause, escalation or time-boxed written counterproposal; do not require termination. The response must avoid accidental acceptance and be specific enough to say live."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck projects at least the quoted position and the proposed negotiated position over a common three-year horizon using maintenance multiples or another transparent normalized baseline.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario table, chart or concise comparison.","grader_hint":"Both scenarios must use the same baseline and period. Dollar values are not required and must not be invented from absent spend data."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Scenario totals and stated savings or differences agree arithmetically with the displayed subscription multiples, escalation assumptions and time horizon.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Displayed calculations and scenario results.","grader_hint":"Recompute the normalized totals. Allow ordinary rounding, but any conclusion about relative cost must follow from the shown assumptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Projection assumptions identify how renewal escalation and one-time migration services are treated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario notes, labels or footnotes.","grader_hint":"The reader must be able to tell whether escalation is applied and whether migration services are included, excluded or shown separately."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The negotiation rationale acknowledges that the eleven-month end-of-support date strengthens the vendor's leverage and responds with credible commercial or delivery controls.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Leverage assessment and negotiating rationale.","grader_hint":"Do not award full credit if the deck portrays the deadline as leverage held by Elmsworth. Look for realistic countermeasures such as conditional commitment, scope control, governance or staged acceptance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The position does not rely on a fabricated competing bid, unsupported market benchmark, invented switching option or threat that the supplied facts do not support.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Negotiation rationale, leverage statements and call language.","grader_hint":"Review factual assertions used to create leverage. Proposed targets are acceptable; purported external facts or alternatives must not be invented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck explicitly distinguishes the relevance of England from that of the Republic of Ireland instead of treating the two jurisdictions as legally identical.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-jurisdiction risk or validation content.","grader_hint":"Look for a concise distinction between the UK framework applicable in England and the EU/Irish framework applicable in the Republic of Ireland."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The jurisdictional framing accurately identifies UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018 for England and EU GDPR with Irish supervisory or implementing context for the Republic of Ireland.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Named legal frameworks or concise jurisdiction labels.","grader_hint":"Equivalent accurate terminology is acceptable. The deck need not cite provisions, but it must not say EU GDPR directly governs England or that UK GDPR governs Irish operations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck does not declare the proposed hosting arrangement compliant or noncompliant while processing locations and final data-protection terms remain unknown.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compliance language and stated validation needs.","grader_hint":"Full credit requires calibrated language such as unresolved, conditional or subject to legal review rather than a definitive legal conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation does not equate data residency with lawful international transfer and identifies transfer arrangements as a separate validation question where relevant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hosting-location and cross-border-transfer discussion.","grader_hint":"Look for recognition that knowing where data is hosted does not by itself resolve transfer legality, access or onward-processing issues."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck does not claim that GDPR or data ownership alone guarantees free, prompt or operationally usable extraction at contract exit.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rationale for contractual exit protections.","grader_hint":"The document should treat extraction format, timing, assistance and fees as matters requiring express contractual protection."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck does not present statutory processor obligations or a data-processing agreement as a substitute for commercial exit, continuity and migration-assistance terms.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Relationship between privacy safeguards and operational contract terms.","grader_hint":"Award full credit when privacy documentation and operational exit rights are treated as complementary but distinct."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Financial authority is bounded correctly: Aleksy may negotiate within the stated envelope but does not purport to approve an over-ceiling commitment or speak for Sasha on unapproved financial exposure.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority labels, escalation points and call roles.","grader_hint":"Check that commitments above 1.75x or outside the defined envelope are reserved for finance approval rather than treated as Aleksy's decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Legal issues are framed as contract requirements, unresolved questions or matters for legal validation, without Aleksy issuing a definitive legal opinion.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legal and privacy wording, ownership and validation labels.","grader_hint":"The deck may state protective terms and identify applicable frameworks, but final conclusions on compliance, transfer mechanisms and contract enforceability must be assigned to legal review."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Any follow-up required before acceptance has a concrete owner and timing tied to the negotiation or the eleven-month migration window.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Owner and timing annotations for finance, legal, technical or vendor actions.","grader_hint":"Look for named roles or supplied people and actionable timing. Vague statements such as 'review later' do not qualify."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation ends on one clear negotiating decision or mandate, not on a list of unresolved next steps or alternative recommendations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final substantive slide and concluding statement.","grader_hint":"The last takeaway must tell Aleksy the position to hold. Supporting actions may appear, but they must not replace or dilute the decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The opening ask, concession ladder, scenario figures, authorised ceiling, walk-away response and non-negotiable agree with one another throughout the presentation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-check of all slides and repeated terms.","grader_hint":"Audit every repeated number and term. A later concession must not exceed the ceiling, contradict the opening package or quietly weaken the declared non-negotiable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Aleksy can use the deck live to open, trade and stop without having to infer missing conditions or invent wording during the call.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall clarity, call language, sequence and decision boundaries.","grader_hint":"Review the artifact as a live-call aid. It should answer what to ask first, what can move next, what must be received in return and when to pause."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck remains a negotiation position memorandum and does not become a general tutorial on ERP hosting, cloud technology or data-protection law.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and proportion of explanatory material.","grader_hint":"Brief explanations needed for Sasha are appropriate; extended background teaching that displaces the position, sequence or decision is not."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Elmsworth Solutions must establish a bounded commercial and technology position before negotiating the forced migration of Ravensmoor Agricultural's operational ERP platform. The presentation will be used live by an IT manager and a non-specialist finance director.","difficulty_sources":["Balancing deadline pressure against commercial discipline when the vendor controls the end-of-support timetable","Pricing concessions by actual value and preserving high-value exit protections until reciprocal movement occurs","Producing internally consistent normalized projections without inventing absent spend data","Distinguishing England and Republic of Ireland data-protection concerns without overstepping into a legal opinion","Giving a non-specialist finance audience an executable live-call position without turning the deck into a tutorial"],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"An information systems manager preparing a bounded position for a live hosted-ERP renewal and migration negotiation, with a non-specialist finance director present.","behaviour_specification":["Convert the known quote of 2.3 times current annual maintenance and the 1.75-times authorised three-year average ceiling into a normalized commercial position without inventing the underlying spend.","Provide one coherent opening package below the authorised ceiling and retain bargaining room.","Design an ordered concession ladder in which low-cost items such as bounded reference-call rights and feasible phased-go-live flexibility are traded first for meaningful vendor movement.","Require reciprocal value at each rung and preserve all negotiable exit-related value until after at least two distinct vendor concessions.","Designate exactly one non-negotiable: practical export of Ravensmoor operational data at exit, in a documented usable format, without a separate extraction fee.","Reject an uncapped renewal escalator while treating the precise finite cap as a commercial position rather than an external fact.","Include a controlled walk-away response that prevents accidental commitment but does not pretend Elmsworth can ignore the approaching end-of-support date.","Compare a quoted-price scenario with a negotiated scenario over three years using a normalized maintenance baseline and explicit escalation and migration-service assumptions.","Separate technology recommendations from finance approval and legal validation.","Distinguish England's UK GDPR and Data Protection Act 2018 context from the Republic of Ireland's EU GDPR and Irish context without making a final compliance determination."],"intended_verdict":"Hold a firm, numerically bounded hosted-migration position rather than accepting deadline pressure. Open below the 1.75x authority ceiling, trade low-cost concessions only for reciprocal vendor improvements, do not spend exit-related flexibility until the vendor has conceded twice, reject uncapped escalation and never move on fee-free usable data export at exit.","gold_relationships":["Let M represent current annual maintenance. The vendor's annual quoted subscription baseline is 2.3M; no currency amount is inferred.","The authorised average annual subscription over three years must not exceed 1.75M, with one-time migration services excluded and separately controlled.","The opening subscription target must be lower than the authorised ceiling and the final permissible position must not exceed it.","Three-year scenario values must equal the sum of annual normalized subscription values after applying the presentation's stated escalation assumption.","Any stated savings must equal the difference between scenarios calculated over the same period and baseline.","Every Elmsworth concession must map to a specific vendor concession.","The first exit-related movement may occur only after two distinct vendor concessions, and the fee-free usable-export core may never be surrendered.","Repeated prices, escalation limits, concession conditions and walk-away boundaries must agree across all slides."],"doctrinal_rule_and_nonclaim_pairs":[{"rule":"England and the Republic of Ireland engage different UK and EU data-protection frameworks.","must_not_claim":"EU GDPR directly governs England or UK GDPR governs processing solely because an Irish site uses the platform."},{"rule":"Unknown processing locations and unfinished contractual terms require legal validation.","must_not_claim":"The proposed hosting arrangement is already compliant or definitively noncompliant."},{"rule":"International-transfer analysis is distinct from the simple location of stored data.","must_not_claim":"Data residency alone establishes lawful transfer or eliminates onward-access risk."},{"rule":"Exit format, timing, assistance and fees require express contractual protection.","must_not_claim":"GDPR, data ownership or access rights automatically provide free and operationally usable extraction."},{"rule":"Privacy processor terms and operational exit protections are complementary.","must_not_claim":"A data-processing agreement or statutory processor duty substitutes for continuity, migration-assistance and commercial exit terms."},{"rule":"Aleksy's authority is bounded by the stated financial envelope and role.","must_not_claim":"Aleksy can approve over-ceiling financial exposure or issue final legal conclusions."}],"reachability_check":"A reference presentation can be produced offline with standard presentation software in five slides or fewer. All numerical checks use supplied multiples and author-stated assumptions; all doctrinal checks rely on stable professional knowledge of IT contracting, data portability, UK/EU privacy boundaries and delegated commercial authority. No rubric item requires an undisclosed local code, live market data or a supplied source.","space_check":"The content can fit within five presentation slides at professional density by combining context and authority, opening package, concession ladder, normalized scenario comparison, and walk-away/jurisdictional boundaries. The rubric does not require each criterion to appear as a separate statement or slide."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"negotiation_position","filename":"negotiation_position.pptx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation","description":"A concise, non-specialist negotiation position memorandum presented as slides for the 22 September hosted-ERP renegotiation call.","required":true,"constraints":["Maximum five slides with no appendix. It must state one opening ask, an ordered concession sequence, a walk-away response, exactly one non-negotiable term, scenario-based commercial implications, and appropriate finance and legal boundaries."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"computer_information_systems_managers","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"The reference solution should be drafted by an experienced IT service and vendor manager, then independently reviewed by one technology-commercial reviewer and one privacy or technology-contract reviewer. Reviewers should verify negotiation usability, normalized financial arithmetic, authority boundaries and the accuracy and restraint of the England/Republic of Ireland treatment.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No vendor contract, data-processing agreement, actual maintenance spend, hosting-location schedule or external market benchmark is supplied. The gold therefore uses normalized maintenance multiples, labels assumptions and avoids a definitive legal-compliance conclusion."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:23+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:23+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:23+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:23+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:35:23+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/e75eca413fc42dd3","declared_deliverables":["negotiation_position.pptx"]};
